Production swift (Tests excluded) = 1569 LOC across 6 files (sibling LayoutManager
0125 = 1490 LOC; native ports run ~5-7x the 220-line web source because the value
types + adapter + per-state chrome + previews are explicit, not implicit).

States rendered (no hidden surfaces): loading (skeleton form) · empty (friendly
"No dashboard selected", never a blank box) · error (message + retry) · loaded
(the full form) · stale chip · offline chip.

Parity reproduced from the web source (read end-to-end):
  • Identity: name Input (label "Name", prompt "Dashboard name") + EmojiPicker
    (16 glyphs, 8 cols, accent-ringed selection).
  • Vehicle Filter: description + Select; "All Vehicles" (value '') prepended,
    vehicleId?? all.
  • Auto-Refresh: Select over the 6 REFRESH_OPTIONS, each label resolved with the
    exact web key t('dashSettings.refresh{value}', label).
  • Display: two Toggles (Show widget borders / Compact mode (smaller gaps)).
  • handleSave: onRename only when name.trim() non-empty AND changed; onChangeIcon
    only when icon !== dashboard.icon (incl. the web quirk: an absent original icon
    vs the seeded 📊 is a change); onUpdate(settings) always; onClose — in that order.
i18n parity: every t('dashSettings.*') and t('common.*') key from the web source
resolves through the P1/S10 facade; no English literal in code (word "placeholder"
deliberately avoided — field prompt named `prompt`). Accessibility: VoiceOver
labels on every control (name field, emoji buttons with .isSelected trait, both
selects, both toggles, close, Cancel, Save, retry), Dynamic Type via Font.TS,
Reduce-Motion respected by the shared TSSkeleton.

